# Deferred work

- Partial setup failure leaks Vulkan objects: if `Renderer::new` fails after
  the swapchain exists (e.g. a `Frame::new` call fails), the swapchain and any
  already-created frames are never destroyed, and neither are the pieces of a
  half-built `Frame` or `Swapchain`. Fix with the deletion queue, so every
  created object is registered for destruction as soon as it exists.
- The triangle pipeline is built for the swapchain's color format. If a
  swapchain recreation ever picks a different format (e.g. the window moves to
  a monitor with other surface formats), the pipeline no longer matches. Goes
  away once scene rendering targets its own fixed-format HDR image.
